      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic batch speech-to-text task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nThe initial file submit_transcription.py is already implemented. Read it before generating the remaining files, and leave it unchanged.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] submit_transcription.py - submits an audio file for batch transcription\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] poll_transcription.py - polls a transcription job and returns the transcript\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] diarized_transcript.py - requests speaker diarization for a recorded meeting\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] timestamped_transcript.py - returns word or segment timestamps from a transcription result\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] speech_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Batch Speech-to-Text\n6. [HELPER] speech_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Batch Speech-to-Text\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] translate_transcript.py - Translate completed transcript segments\n8. [LATER-STEP] moderate_transcript.py - Moderate transcript text before publishing\n9. [LATER-STEP] archive_summary.py - Summarize transcription results\n10. [LATER-STEP] transcript_embedding.py - Embed transcript segments for semantic retrieval\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
